---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ"
  description="Current answers about pfseeker browsing, planned content types, hosting, collections, submissions, and reporting."
>
  <section class="page-shell prose-page" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h1 id="faq-title">Current project answers</h1>
      <p>
        These answers reflect the site as it exists now and clearly mark planned
        features.
      </p>
    </div>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-one">
      <h2 id="faq-one">What is pfseeker?</h2>
      <p>
        pfseeker is being built as a curated discovery platform for profile
        pictures, banners, icons, and visual collections.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-two">
      <h2 id="faq-two">Does browsing require an account?</h2>
      <p>
        No. Public browsing remains useful without an account. Discord sign-in
        is available for account identity and uses the Discord <code
          >identify</code
        >
        scope only. pfseeker does not require a Discord server membership, bot, role,
        or email address.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-three">
      <h2 id="faq-three">How will images be hosted?</h2>
      <p>
        Media delivery is planned around Cloudinary for responsive previews,
        transformations, and original downloads.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-four">
      <h2 id="faq-four">How will collections work?</h2>
      <p>
        Collections require Discord sign-in. Signed-in users can create multiple
        private collections, save assets from gallery and detail pages, reorder
        items, remove items, and download a collection ZIP. Anonymous visitors
        can still browse, search, preview, and download individual assets.
      </p>
      <p>
        This behavior has been manually verified in production. Public
        collection publishing is not enabled yet.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-five">
      <h2 id="faq-five">Can users submit images?</h2>
      <p>
        Signed-in users can submit PFP, banner, and icon images into a private
        pending state. Accepted formats are JPG, JPEG, PNG, WebP, and GIF.
        Category, existing tags, suggested tags, source URL, and creator credit
        fields are optional, and there is no guarantee of publication.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pending submissions are stored through Cloudinary and shown only to the
        submitting account until moderation. On the Phase 13 feature branch,
        moderators can approve and publish, reject, or correct metadata. Pending
        submissions can be cancelled by the submitter. Approved, published, and
        rejected submissions cannot be cancelled by the submitter.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="faq-six">
      <h2 id="faq-six">How will copyright or reports work?</h2>
      <p>
        Moderation workflows are implemented on the Phase 13 feature branch.
        Report workflows remain planned and are not available yet. Current
        submissions require users to confirm that images do not contain obvious
        nudity, gore or graphic injury, or hateful imagery.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
